Relax the CUDA-vs-CPU tolerance for affine transformations of bounding boxes.

The torchvision test suite can fail for rotated float32 bounding boxes because
CUDA and CPU calculations differ slightly in the resulting angle. Use the
tolerance adopted upstream (atol=1e-5, rtol=1e-5), which is sufficient for the
observed numerical difference without weakening the functional test.

Backport of upstream commit:
https://github.com/pytorch/vision/commit/ca2212438fdd8ce29b66999ed70ed54b0f9372d1

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
--- a/test/test_transforms_v2.py
+++ b/test/test_transforms_v2.py
@@ -1439,6 +1439,7 @@ class TestAffine:
             canvas_size=bounding_boxes.canvas_size,
             **{param: value},
             check_scripted_vs_eager=not (param == "shear" and isinstance(value, (int, float))),
+            check_cuda_vs_cpu=dict(atol=1e-5, rtol=1e-5),
         )
